Pick aes-ni.c's _mm_setr_epi8 for any GCC-compatible compiler.

MM_SETR_EPI8 uses _mm_setr_epi8 only under _WIN64, falling back to a brace
initialiser that is correct for MSVC's __m128i (a byte union) but fills
clang's and GCC's (a two-lane vector) wrongly -- the AES-NI SDCTR bug this
port fixed for 6.5.8, which upstream's _WIN64 condition fixed only for
Win64. Any compiler defining __GNUC__ (clang does) now takes the intrinsic.
(The clang pragma's pop, once in this patch, is upstream since winscp/winscp#72.)
Line counts are unchanged.

--- a/source/putty/crypto/aes-ni.c	2026-10-11 18:42:14.225530897 -0300
+++ b/source/putty/crypto/aes-ni.c	2026-10-11 18:42:14.243297762 -0300
@@ -126,7 +126,7 @@
 // And consequently the code crashes.
 // This macro is based on:
 // https://stackoverflow.com/q/35268036/850848
-#ifdef _WIN64
+#if defined(_WIN64) || defined(__GNUC__) // linscp: the brace form is for MSVC, not clang or GCC
 #define MM_SETR_EPI8(a0, a1, a2, a3, a4, a5, a6, a7, a8, a9, aa, ab, ac, ad, ae, af) \
     _mm_setr_epi8(a0, a1, a2, a3, a4, a5, a6, a7, a8, a9, aa, ab, ac, ad, ae, af)
 #else
